To access a form after clicking a button in HTML and CSS, you need to use JavaScript to create an event listener for the button click. Then, you can manipulate the visibility or display property of the form using JavaScript or CSS.

Here's an example of how to do this with JavaScript:

HTML:

```
<button id="showFormBtn">Show Form </button>
<form id="form" style="display:none;">
  <!-- form elements here -->
</form>

```

JavaScript:

```
const btn = document.getElementById("showFormBtn");
const form = document.getElementById("form");

btn.addEventListener("click", function() {
  form.style.display = "block";
});

```

This will make the form become visible when the button is clicked.
